            <div xml:id="d954">

                <pb facs="0995" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg875"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/197:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-26T11:00:00-05:45">May 26, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. I am awaiting a reply to my 74, May 22 [<hi rendition="#italic">12</hi>], 3
                    p.m., before taking up with President Moncada the designation of Major Price. I
                    have just learned that President Moncada is considering the appointment of Dr.
                    Aguado, the Vice President, as chairman of the National Board of Elections and
                    Dr. Aguado has expressed a desire to consult me in this matter. Please
                    instruct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
